WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.003 --> 00:00:01.838
Harry: From calorie
count to portion sizes,

00:00:01.838 --> 00:00:03.240
we wanted to find out all the differences

00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:06.109
between Lay's and Walkers
in the US and the UK.

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:07.644
This is "Food Wars."

00:00:09.513 --> 00:00:10.347
We'll start with a quick note

00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:11.681
to explain their different names.

00:00:11.681 --> 00:00:13.016
Walkers used to be its own company

00:00:13.016 --> 00:00:15.152
and was the most popular
crisp brand in the UK.

00:00:15.152 --> 00:00:17.654
Frito-Lay actually
acquired Walkers in 1989,

00:00:17.654 --> 00:00:19.689
but they decided to still
use the brand name in the UK

00:00:19.689 --> 00:00:21.625
so all that brand loyalty
didn't go to waste.

00:00:21.625 --> 00:00:24.327
In the UK, Walkers crisps
come in five portion sizes.

00:00:24.327 --> 00:00:26.229
A multipack 25-gram bag,

00:00:26.229 --> 00:00:28.031
a 32.5-gram bag,

00:00:28.031 --> 00:00:29.366
a 45-gram bag,

00:00:29.366 --> 00:00:30.801
a 65-gram bag,

00:00:30.801 --> 00:00:33.403
and a 175-gram sharing bag.

00:00:33.403 --> 00:00:37.240
The smallest that's in the
multipack bag is 28 grams.

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.409
Then we move up to a 78-gram bag,

00:00:39.409 --> 00:00:41.545
a 226-gram bag,

00:00:41.545 --> 00:00:46.016
and then our party-size bag, 368 grams.

00:00:46.016 --> 00:00:49.853
That means our biggest bag is 110% larger

00:00:49.853 --> 00:00:52.322
than the biggest bag in the UK.

00:00:52.322 --> 00:00:53.256
A few other things to note.

00:00:53.256 --> 00:00:54.925
In the UK, if you get a flavored bag,

00:00:54.925 --> 00:00:56.960
it's the same weight as
the ready-salted version.

00:00:56.960 --> 00:00:58.862
Whereas in the US, our flavored bags

00:00:58.862 --> 00:01:00.597
weigh less than the
original-flavored bags.

00:01:00.597 --> 00:01:04.034
Take this bag of salt and vinegar chips.

00:01:04.034 --> 00:01:06.169
It weighs 7.75 ounces,

00:01:06.169 --> 00:01:10.006
compared to the classic
regular-salted 8-ounce bag.

00:01:10.006 --> 00:01:13.076
Back in 2014, PepsiCo claimed the reason

00:01:13.076 --> 00:01:15.212
there is a slightly higher price per ounce

00:01:15.212 --> 00:01:17.581
for flavored chips is the added seasoning.

00:01:17.581 --> 00:01:19.316
OK, before we continue,

00:01:19.316 --> 00:01:21.852
they're telling us,
"Weighs less, costs more

00:01:21.852 --> 00:01:24.154
because we're adding more
seasoning." Right, guys?

00:01:24.154 --> 00:01:26.456
Well, I got a question for you, PepsiCo.

00:01:26.456 --> 00:01:27.891
[grunting]

00:01:27.891 --> 00:01:29.159
What does that say there?

00:01:29.159 --> 00:01:30.527
Says "Lightly Salted."

00:01:30.527 --> 00:01:33.663
So I understand this has
less salt than these guys?

00:01:33.663 --> 00:01:34.931
Huh.

00:01:34.931 --> 00:01:38.969
Closer inspection: right
there, 7 3/4 ounces.

00:01:38.969 --> 00:01:40.303
Not the full 8.

00:01:40.303 --> 00:01:43.240
If there's less seasoning
and salt in here,

00:01:43.240 --> 00:01:46.243
why is it a smaller
ounce and a higher price?

00:01:47.477 --> 00:01:48.979
They're stealing my salt!

00:01:48.979 --> 00:01:51.615
Salt, literally the cheapest
thing on the planet.

00:01:51.615 --> 00:01:53.149
We have a whole ocean full of it,

00:01:53.149 --> 00:01:55.485
and yet they're still skimping on it!

00:01:57.020 --> 00:01:58.788
Your move, PepsiCo.

00:01:58.788 --> 00:02:02.692
This 28-gram bag of chips
supposedly has 15 chips in it,

00:02:02.692 --> 00:02:04.794
according to Lay's website.

00:02:04.794 --> 00:02:06.463
Well, they lied about the salt,

00:02:06.463 --> 00:02:07.597
what else are they lying about?

00:02:07.597 --> 00:02:08.431
I'm going to count the crisps

00:02:08.431 --> 00:02:10.200
in this 25-gram bag for comparison.

00:02:10.200 --> 00:02:11.401
These chips are demolished.

00:02:13.103 --> 00:02:14.538
I feel like it's more than 15.

00:02:14.538 --> 00:02:15.805
This is what we call the

00:02:15.805 --> 00:02:18.141
stoner-math section of "Food Wars."

00:02:18.141 --> 00:02:20.377
We do the math so you
stoners don't have to.

00:02:20.377 --> 00:02:22.913
All right. So, one, two.

00:02:22.913 --> 00:02:24.481
That's a whole one.

00:02:24.481 --> 00:02:25.348
Little peephole.

00:02:25.348 --> 00:02:27.717
Absolute Frankenstein of a crisp, this.

00:02:27.717 --> 00:02:31.721
Arguably not one
put-together chip in here.

00:02:31.721 --> 00:02:32.956
OK, let's just ...

00:02:32.956 --> 00:02:35.659
that's a chip, that's a chip, right?

00:02:35.659 --> 00:02:36.927
So, the issue there is that the crisps

00:02:36.927 --> 00:02:38.628
are all vastly different sizes.

00:02:38.628 --> 00:02:41.264
Like, this one, just one
crisp, but it's tiny,

00:02:41.264 --> 00:02:43.600
whereas this one, also
one crisp, but way bigger.

00:02:43.600 --> 00:02:46.036
And we've ended up with 22.

00:02:46.036 --> 00:02:48.204
Of all the arbitrary
things we do on this show,

00:02:48.204 --> 00:02:49.906
this has to be the most arbitrary.

00:02:49.906 --> 00:02:51.141
Wow, look at that, everyone!

00:02:51.141 --> 00:02:52.642
They gave me an extra chip.

00:02:52.642 --> 00:02:54.611
16 instead of 15.

00:02:54.611 --> 00:02:55.545
The last thing we wanted to check

00:02:55.545 --> 00:02:57.147
was how much air you're
getting in your bags.

00:02:57.147 --> 00:02:58.915
Walkers in the UK are kind of notorious

00:02:58.915 --> 00:03:00.817
for seemingly underfilling the bags.

00:03:00.817 --> 00:03:02.452
We're going to find the volume of the bag

00:03:02.452 --> 00:03:04.321
and then the volume of the crisps inside

00:03:04.321 --> 00:03:06.389
to find out just how much
wasted space there is.

00:03:06.389 --> 00:03:09.893
What I need to do is
carefully open the bag

00:03:09.893 --> 00:03:11.061
just enough to let the air out,

00:03:11.061 --> 00:03:13.296
and then I'm going to
try and powder these,

00:03:13.296 --> 00:03:15.198
like just crush them as far as I can,

00:03:15.198 --> 00:03:18.134
and then measure the volume
of the powder in this thing.

00:03:18.134 --> 00:03:21.404
First I gotta crumble it up.

00:03:21.404 --> 00:03:23.006
[whispering] Crushing bags with Harry.

00:03:23.006 --> 00:03:25.542
[bag crackling]

00:03:25.542 --> 00:03:28.211
Oh, this is like ... [growls].

00:03:29.980 --> 00:03:31.247
It's quite therapeutic.

00:03:31.247 --> 00:03:33.450
It feels like I'm giving a massage.

00:03:33.450 --> 00:03:35.318
Just, like, the world's worst massage.

00:03:39.623 --> 00:03:41.458
I need something to kind of tamp it down,

00:03:41.458 --> 00:03:43.493
'cause the air is stuck in
there, so I'll just use,

00:03:43.493 --> 00:03:44.494
oh, I don't know,

00:03:44.494 --> 00:03:46.196
this pair of nunchucks!

00:03:51.401 --> 00:03:52.335
Oh, yeah!

00:03:54.304 --> 00:03:55.739
Now, step two is going to be

00:03:55.739 --> 00:03:57.407
to find the volume of the bag itself.

00:03:57.407 --> 00:03:59.242
So we're going to fill the bag with water

00:03:59.242 --> 00:04:01.144
to try and find the volume.

00:04:01.144 --> 00:04:02.545
Oh, God. Oh.

00:04:02.545 --> 00:04:03.813
Tiny bit more.

00:04:03.813 --> 00:04:04.614
Perfect.

00:04:04.614 --> 00:04:06.516
Sarah: OK. We did it!

00:04:06.516 --> 00:04:07.784
But now I have to get it in there

00:04:07.784 --> 00:04:10.353
without spilling it everywhere.

00:04:10.353 --> 00:04:11.621
Three, two, one, go.

00:04:11.621 --> 00:04:13.256
[laughing]

00:04:13.256 --> 00:04:15.091
Sarah: Oh, that is perfect!

00:04:15.091 --> 00:04:15.925
Harry: Look at that!

00:04:15.925 --> 00:04:17.127
That went pretty well.

00:04:17.127 --> 00:04:18.895
We didn't spill water everywhere.

00:04:20.964 --> 00:04:22.332
Oh, my God, it's, like,
right to the top there.

00:04:22.332 --> 00:04:23.933
That's crazy how that worked. OK.

00:04:23.933 --> 00:04:25.935
Buchi and Wumi are making
a triumphant return.

00:04:25.935 --> 00:04:28.238
Go and watch the Oreos episode
if you haven't already.

00:04:29.406 --> 00:04:30.974
Some of that,

00:04:30.974 --> 00:04:33.343
and then measure the rest.

00:04:33.343 --> 00:04:35.445
Y'all brought number two!

00:04:37.147 --> 00:04:38.348
[laughing] Oh, God.

00:04:38.348 --> 00:04:40.583
Can you see the bits of stuff
floating around in there?

00:04:40.583 --> 00:04:41.885
So, according to my trusted friend

00:04:41.885 --> 00:04:43.420
PercentageCalculator.net,

00:04:43.420 --> 00:04:47.691
around 90% of a 25-gram
Walkers bag is wasted space.

00:04:47.691 --> 00:04:48.925
I don't know what the math is

00:04:48.925 --> 00:04:51.227
I'm supposed to be figuring out, I forgot,

00:04:51.227 --> 00:04:54.664
but whoever's editing this,
take all those numbers,

00:04:54.664 --> 00:04:56.966
and this is the conclusion.

00:04:56.966 --> 00:05:00.236
Now, that air is actually
there for a reason.

00:05:00.236 --> 00:05:02.672
It's nitrogen gas, which
helps preserve the chips

00:05:02.672 --> 00:05:03.907
and also acts as a cushion

00:05:03.907 --> 00:05:06.076
to stop them getting smashed in transit.

00:05:06.076 --> 00:05:07.610
I mean, imagine what it'd be like

00:05:07.610 --> 00:05:08.845
if it didn't have all that air in there.

00:05:08.845 --> 00:05:11.014
So, as much air as there is in there,

00:05:11.014 --> 00:05:12.115
it's actually vitally important.

00:05:12.115 --> 00:05:13.650
If anything, they should put
more air in these things,

00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:15.719
'cause these things, they turn into dust.

00:05:15.719 --> 00:05:17.020
Into dust!

00:05:18.621 --> 00:05:20.256
Here are all the Walkers
products from the UK

00:05:20.256 --> 00:05:21.858
that you won't find in the US.

00:05:21.858 --> 00:05:24.561
And here is everything
you can only get in the US

00:05:24.561 --> 00:05:26.062
and not in the UK.

00:05:26.062 --> 00:05:29.232
I am losing my mind, let's go!

00:05:29.232 --> 00:05:30.133
I want to start with a couple

00:05:30.133 --> 00:05:32.135
of linguistic/stylistic differences

00:05:32.135 --> 00:05:33.236
rather than anything else.

00:05:33.236 --> 00:05:34.971
For example, in the UK,

00:05:34.971 --> 00:05:37.841
we call our classic Walkers ready salted,

00:05:37.841 --> 00:05:39.275
as opposed to original.

00:05:39.275 --> 00:05:43.379
I believe this is a reference
to the very old days of crisps

00:05:43.379 --> 00:05:44.614
where what you would actually get

00:05:44.614 --> 00:05:46.416
is just, like, a bag of plain crisps,

00:05:46.416 --> 00:05:48.084
and then you would have
to add your own salt.

00:05:48.084 --> 00:05:49.452
These ones are ready salted.

00:05:49.452 --> 00:05:51.054
You don't have to add any
salt, it's already on there.

00:05:51.054 --> 00:05:52.689
One stylistic difference
that's worth pointing out

00:05:52.689 --> 00:05:55.959
is that in the UK, our salt
and vinegar chips are green.

00:05:55.959 --> 00:05:59.529
I will say Walkers is kind of
the only brand that does that.

00:05:59.529 --> 00:06:01.331
And then we're on to some
actual exclusive flavors.

00:06:01.331 --> 00:06:04.234
We'll start with this one,
which is cheese and onion.

00:06:04.234 --> 00:06:05.702
Now, Americans don't
have cheese and onion,

00:06:05.702 --> 00:06:07.170
which might shock a few Brits

00:06:07.170 --> 00:06:08.705
because it's one of the
most popular flavors here.

00:06:08.705 --> 00:06:11.174
Instead they have I think,
like, cheddar and sour cream

00:06:11.174 --> 00:06:12.542
and sour cream and onion.

00:06:12.542 --> 00:06:13.777
It just ruins your breath.

00:06:13.777 --> 00:06:15.712
Your breath smells so bad after these.

00:06:15.712 --> 00:06:17.147
How did I get so lucky?

00:06:17.147 --> 00:06:19.315
I love chips, I love different flavors,

00:06:19.315 --> 00:06:21.751
I love trying new varieties,
and I hate paying for it.

00:06:21.751 --> 00:06:24.020
So this is perfect for me.

00:06:24.020 --> 00:06:25.588
I'm going to start with a flavor

00:06:25.588 --> 00:06:28.124
that I never even heard
of, cheddar jalapeño.

00:06:29.359 --> 00:06:31.427
Oh, my God!

00:06:32.695 --> 00:06:34.130
I like the kick on these.

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:35.865
It reminds me of the
cheddar and sour cream,

00:06:35.865 --> 00:06:37.300
which I can't believe you guys don't have.

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:40.503
This flavor took over about 20 years ago,

00:06:40.503 --> 00:06:43.873
and I don't know why it's
so good, but it is good!

00:06:43.873 --> 00:06:44.741
Love this flavor.

00:06:44.741 --> 00:06:45.575
If I had to rank them though,

00:06:45.575 --> 00:06:47.410
I'll put the jalapeño above that one,

00:06:47.410 --> 00:06:48.611
the cheddar and sour cream.

00:06:48.611 --> 00:06:50.046
Sour cream and onion, I
don't even got to open these.

00:06:50.046 --> 00:06:52.048
Sour cream and onion, classic flavor.

00:06:52.048 --> 00:06:54.584
I mean, barbecue in America is amazing.

00:06:54.584 --> 00:06:56.886
I mean, this is just a
classic, classic flavor.

00:06:58.488 --> 00:06:59.923
Oh, man. Fantastic.

00:06:59.923 --> 00:07:03.560
But how does that compare to
sweet Southern heat barbecue?

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.028
Southern heat!

00:07:06.763 --> 00:07:07.597
Oh, yeah.

00:07:07.597 --> 00:07:08.965
I put these above these.

00:07:08.965 --> 00:07:10.366
Then we got honey barbecue.

00:07:10.366 --> 00:07:11.935
How sweet is this one going to be?

00:07:13.303 --> 00:07:14.904
You got greedy with the sweetness.

00:07:14.904 --> 00:07:16.306
Ooh, chili lime.

00:07:16.306 --> 00:07:18.074
Yeah, dude. I've never had these before.

00:07:18.074 --> 00:07:19.475
Chilies and limes.

00:07:19.475 --> 00:07:20.677
See that? Chilies, limes.

00:07:20.677 --> 00:07:22.278
Fantastic combination.

00:07:23.646 --> 00:07:24.948
Ooh, I don't know how I feel about these.

00:07:24.948 --> 00:07:26.216
It's like, I wasn't into them before,

00:07:26.216 --> 00:07:27.584
but now I kind of can't stop eating them.

00:07:27.584 --> 00:07:28.785
Another iconic British flavor

00:07:28.785 --> 00:07:30.987
that's also exclusive is prawn cocktail.

00:07:30.987 --> 00:07:33.156
Brits became really
obsessed with prawn cocktail

00:07:33.156 --> 00:07:35.058
in, like, the '70s, I think it was.

00:07:35.058 --> 00:07:36.626
It just became a sort of trendy thing

00:07:36.626 --> 00:07:37.894
to serve at dinner parties.

00:07:37.894 --> 00:07:39.863
I'm not mad about that, because
it is a really tasty one.

00:07:39.863 --> 00:07:41.931
It just kind of tastes tomatoey,

00:07:41.931 --> 00:07:43.633
because it was usually served with

00:07:43.633 --> 00:07:46.936
a tomato mayo-Worcestershire
sauce combination.

00:07:46.936 --> 00:07:48.705
Next we've got a personal
favorite of mine,

00:07:48.705 --> 00:07:50.440
which is Marmite crisps.

00:07:50.440 --> 00:07:52.375
God, I love Marmite. Marmite is fantastic.

00:07:52.375 --> 00:07:54.577
The slogan was, "You either
love it or you hate it,"

00:07:54.577 --> 00:07:56.512
and it does still ring true,
I think, for most people.

00:07:56.512 --> 00:07:57.914
I'm firmly in the love-it camp.

00:07:59.983 --> 00:08:02.018
Bit of tang from the amount
of salt that's in there.

00:08:02.018 --> 00:08:03.086
Fantastic crisp.

00:08:03.086 --> 00:08:06.456
Harry was nice enough to send
me some of his UK exclusives,

00:08:06.456 --> 00:08:07.590
which I'm going to look at right now.

00:08:07.590 --> 00:08:08.491
Where do I want to start?

00:08:08.491 --> 00:08:10.526
I guess all start — oh, no.

00:08:10.526 --> 00:08:11.594
Marmite.

00:08:11.594 --> 00:08:13.663
I don't get why people love Marmite.

00:08:17.901 --> 00:08:19.369
Ugh!

00:08:20.837 --> 00:08:22.672
I mean, it tastes exactly like ass.

00:08:22.672 --> 00:08:23.640
I hear millennials like that,

00:08:23.640 --> 00:08:24.974
so maybe that's a selling point for them.

00:08:24.974 --> 00:08:26.676
They should actually be
like, "Tastes like ass,"

00:08:26.676 --> 00:08:30.346
'cause the kids are into that
these days, but I am not.

00:08:30.346 --> 00:08:31.714
Then we have a couple of meaty options,

00:08:31.714 --> 00:08:33.917
which I'm surprised you guys
don't have in the States.

00:08:33.917 --> 00:08:36.286
We kind of love combining
crisps and meat, as it seems,

00:08:36.286 --> 00:08:39.222
starting with these roast chicken crisps.

00:08:39.222 --> 00:08:42.191
Another meaty option is
these, which is smoky bacon.

00:08:42.191 --> 00:08:43.493
Then we have these ones,

00:08:43.493 --> 00:08:45.728
which are tomato-ketchup-flavored Walkers.

00:08:47.797 --> 00:08:50.667
In my opinion, prawn cocktail does ketchup

00:08:50.667 --> 00:08:52.035
better than ketchup does ketchup.

00:08:52.035 --> 00:08:53.937
And then for the last of
our standard crisp flavors,

00:08:53.937 --> 00:08:54.971
we have pickled onion.

00:08:54.971 --> 00:08:55.872
Pickled onion's another thing

00:08:55.872 --> 00:08:57.240
that's kind of iconic to British culture

00:08:57.240 --> 00:08:59.742
in the same way that maybe
prawn cocktail or Marmite are,

00:08:59.742 --> 00:09:00.777
just 'cause it's quite traditional

00:09:00.777 --> 00:09:03.980
to find a big jar of pickled
onions or pickled eggs in pubs,

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:05.615
and you'd have one of those as a bar snack

00:09:05.615 --> 00:09:06.649
while you're drinking your pint.

00:09:08.284 --> 00:09:10.053
The complaint I often have against pickles

00:09:10.053 --> 00:09:12.055
and pickled onions is that
they're not tangy enough.

00:09:12.055 --> 00:09:14.590
And these are very tangy,
so good job, Walkers.

00:09:17.794 --> 00:09:19.195
Puckering pickled onion.

00:09:19.195 --> 00:09:20.596
What does that mean?

00:09:20.596 --> 00:09:23.266
Puckering? Like [makes kissing sound]?

00:09:23.266 --> 00:09:26.769
Like I'm being kissed by a pickled onion?

00:09:26.769 --> 00:09:28.104
Yo, these suck!

00:09:29.138 --> 00:09:30.506
Hey, Joe, can I try some of those?

00:09:30.506 --> 00:09:33.176
Hey, Harry, try some of
these great American flavors!

00:09:38.381 --> 00:09:39.615
Thank you!

00:09:40.650 --> 00:09:41.651
Let's start with the limón.

00:09:41.651 --> 00:09:42.952
That's what I've got in my hand.

00:09:46.656 --> 00:09:48.624
Ooh, those are lemony!

00:09:48.624 --> 00:09:49.459
Whew!

00:09:49.459 --> 00:09:50.860
I don't think I've ever
had a citrus crisp before.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:52.228
That is not something
that we have in the UK.

00:09:52.228 --> 00:09:53.162
Those are good.

00:09:53.162 --> 00:09:55.999
I gotta say, love these chips.

00:09:55.999 --> 00:09:56.966
Yeah.

00:09:56.966 --> 00:09:58.501
I got to score a bag of these.

00:09:58.501 --> 00:10:02.805
Chesapeake Bay crab seasoning Lay's.

00:10:03.906 --> 00:10:05.641
Uh-oh!

00:10:05.641 --> 00:10:06.476
Yuelei: No?

00:10:06.476 --> 00:10:08.244
Yeah, no, these are bad.
Put these at the bottom.

00:10:08.244 --> 00:10:10.780
These are at my 7-Eleven.

00:10:10.780 --> 00:10:13.116
Tomato-and-chili-flavored
chips, which sounds amazing.

00:10:13.116 --> 00:10:15.952
I'm going to pronounce
this wrong. Sabritas?

00:10:15.952 --> 00:10:17.387
Adobadas.

00:10:17.387 --> 00:10:18.588
"Hecho en Mexico."

00:10:20.623 --> 00:10:22.025
Oh, yeah, dude!

00:10:22.025 --> 00:10:23.326
Not that spicy. They remind me kind of

00:10:23.326 --> 00:10:24.994
a little bit like Takis.

00:10:24.994 --> 00:10:26.095
Look how red this is.

00:10:26.095 --> 00:10:27.897
Don't you think they'd be super spicy?

00:10:27.897 --> 00:10:28.731
I like that.

00:10:28.731 --> 00:10:29.632
These chip brands,

00:10:29.632 --> 00:10:31.134
they're all going after
each other's throats.

00:10:31.134 --> 00:10:34.504
It is really just like guerrilla warfare.

00:10:34.504 --> 00:10:36.205
You guys don't understand what's going on

00:10:36.205 --> 00:10:37.974
in our grocery stores in this country.

00:10:37.974 --> 00:10:41.778
This is an uneasy mafia
alliance in Chip City.

00:10:44.914 --> 00:10:46.849
No.

00:10:46.849 --> 00:10:49.118
Because when it's thin like these,

00:10:49.118 --> 00:10:50.686
it brings out the flavor more,

00:10:50.686 --> 00:10:52.488
if that makes sense, and it's too strong.

00:10:54.457 --> 00:10:56.259
It turns out if you put
Doritos Cool Ranch seasoning

00:10:56.259 --> 00:10:57.593
on anything, it'll taste good.

00:10:57.593 --> 00:10:59.362
Dill pickle.

00:10:59.362 --> 00:11:00.630
So, I hate pickles.

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:01.664
Oof.

00:11:04.801 --> 00:11:07.036
[groaning]

00:11:07.036 --> 00:11:07.970
I hate them!

00:11:07.970 --> 00:11:09.839
Put these at the bottom of every list.

00:11:09.839 --> 00:11:11.774
I don't know what the
Flamin' Hot dill pickle chips

00:11:11.774 --> 00:11:13.843
taste like, but the
regular dill pickle chips

00:11:13.843 --> 00:11:15.511
are absolutely disgusting.

00:11:15.511 --> 00:11:17.013
These sound phenomenal.

00:11:17.013 --> 00:11:19.515
Flamin' Hot dill-pickle-flavored crisps.

00:11:22.385 --> 00:11:23.586
Match made in heaven for me.

00:11:23.586 --> 00:11:25.655
You get the heat, you get
that little bit of tang

00:11:25.655 --> 00:11:27.190
to kind of cut through it.

00:11:27.190 --> 00:11:28.624
If I could take one of these four

00:11:28.624 --> 00:11:31.761
and have them in the UK
permanently, these ones.

00:11:31.761 --> 00:11:33.396
One thing Walkers utilize a lot in the UK

00:11:33.396 --> 00:11:34.764
are promotional flavors.

00:11:34.764 --> 00:11:36.065
So currently what they've got going on

00:11:36.065 --> 00:11:36.999
is one where they've partnered

00:11:36.999 --> 00:11:38.801
with four different
restaurants from around the UK

00:11:38.801 --> 00:11:40.536
to showcase some different cuisines.

00:11:40.536 --> 00:11:42.071
So that means that we now have

00:11:42.071 --> 00:11:43.706
fish-and-chip-flavored Walkers,

00:11:43.706 --> 00:11:45.675
Madras-curry-flavored Walkers,

00:11:45.675 --> 00:11:47.343
Thai-green-curry-flavored Walkers,

00:11:47.343 --> 00:11:49.145
and chicken burrito Walkers.

00:11:49.145 --> 00:11:51.948
At one point they made
a Cajun squirrel flavor.

00:11:51.948 --> 00:11:52.949
I'm not making that up.

00:11:52.949 --> 00:11:55.885
This one looks really
good. Thai green curry?

00:11:55.885 --> 00:11:57.520
Think I'm gonna like this.

00:11:58.688 --> 00:12:00.790
Yuck. Yuck!

00:12:00.790 --> 00:12:01.757
Rank them down.

00:12:01.757 --> 00:12:02.658
Fish and chips. OK.

00:12:02.658 --> 00:12:04.160
I like fish and chips. Hang on.

00:12:04.160 --> 00:12:05.561
It smells like cat food.

00:12:05.561 --> 00:12:07.763
Now I can't stop thinking
about dry cat food.

00:12:07.763 --> 00:12:09.198
All right. I like fish and chips.

00:12:15.204 --> 00:12:16.772
This is the worst one.

00:12:16.772 --> 00:12:18.141
This is so — [choking].

00:12:18.141 --> 00:12:19.175
I'm gonna throw up.

00:12:20.576 --> 00:12:24.280
Crown it. This is the
worst chip I've ever eaten,

00:12:24.280 --> 00:12:25.948
the worst chip I've ever reviewed,

00:12:25.948 --> 00:12:28.818
and this might be the worst
thing I've ever tasted.

00:12:28.818 --> 00:12:30.853
Like, I feel like I'm on a prank show.

00:12:30.853 --> 00:12:32.488
"We farted in a bag, gotcha!"

00:12:32.488 --> 00:12:34.223
Like, oh, you know, like —

00:12:34.223 --> 00:12:36.259
In the UK, Walkers has
a range of Baked crisps,

00:12:36.259 --> 00:12:37.193
which I guess are marketed as

00:12:37.193 --> 00:12:38.528
kind of like a healthier option.

00:12:38.528 --> 00:12:39.996
These come in four flavors:

00:12:39.996 --> 00:12:42.965
salt and vinegar, cheese and onion,

00:12:42.965 --> 00:12:46.235
sour cream and onion, prawn cocktail.

00:12:46.235 --> 00:12:48.104
We also have Baked potato chip options,

00:12:48.104 --> 00:12:49.505
and one Baked flavor you can get here

00:12:49.505 --> 00:12:53.676
you can't get it in the UK
is this, the barbecue Baked.

00:12:53.676 --> 00:12:54.510
Besides the Baked,

00:12:54.510 --> 00:12:56.479
there are also these
other healthier options

00:12:56.479 --> 00:12:58.481
for Lay's potato chips fans.

00:12:58.481 --> 00:13:01.851
It's known as the Better for
You range of potato chips,

00:13:01.851 --> 00:13:02.852
and you can't get them in the UK.

00:13:02.852 --> 00:13:05.555
You can get them here in
the US, including these,

00:13:05.555 --> 00:13:08.357
the before-mentioned lightly salted chips.

00:13:08.357 --> 00:13:10.993
Besides these, you can get
lightly salted barbecue,

00:13:10.993 --> 00:13:14.964
wavy lightly salted,
Simply sea salt thick-cut,

00:13:14.964 --> 00:13:16.832
and Simply barbecue thick-cut.

00:13:16.832 --> 00:13:19.202
If you like crunchy chips,
Lay's also has you covered.

00:13:19.202 --> 00:13:21.537
They have their Kettle Cooked series.

00:13:21.537 --> 00:13:24.373
Here's four of the
flavors that I could find.

00:13:24.373 --> 00:13:25.608
Original.

00:13:25.608 --> 00:13:27.743
Flamin' Hot. You guys
want me to open these?

00:13:29.378 --> 00:13:30.746
[laughing]

00:13:30.746 --> 00:13:31.914
These are so red.

00:13:31.914 --> 00:13:33.549
These win the reddest-chip award.

00:13:33.549 --> 00:13:34.450
Look how red these are.

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:36.619
Like my eyes. Ahh!

00:13:38.621 --> 00:13:40.389
I like the flavor of these,
but they're not very hot.

00:13:40.389 --> 00:13:41.958
Oh, wait, yeah, they are. Ooh, yeah.

00:13:41.958 --> 00:13:44.293
Oh, man, the Kettle Cooked jalapeño.

00:13:44.293 --> 00:13:45.595
I think this whole kettle-chip thing

00:13:45.595 --> 00:13:47.563
was just a ruse to go after Miss Vickie's.

00:13:49.732 --> 00:13:51.534
Yep. They're, like, really similar.

00:13:51.534 --> 00:13:53.002
And I love those Miss Vickie chips.

00:13:53.002 --> 00:13:54.270
Sea salt and vinegar.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:56.472
Sea salt and cracked pepper.

00:13:56.472 --> 00:13:58.507
Other Kettle Cooked flavors
I could not get my hands on

00:13:58.507 --> 00:14:01.344
include the mesquite
barbecue, the Maui onion —

00:14:01.344 --> 00:14:02.745
oh, I would have loved those —

00:14:02.745 --> 00:14:05.348
and, of course, the reduced-fat original.

00:14:05.348 --> 00:14:06.182
Sorry.

00:14:06.182 --> 00:14:08.517
We'll start with this one,
which is Max Punchy Paprika.

00:14:08.517 --> 00:14:09.885
Now, I'm surprised you
guys don't have more

00:14:09.885 --> 00:14:11.454
paprika-flavored crisps in the US,

00:14:11.454 --> 00:14:12.555
'cause it's a really good flavor.

00:14:12.555 --> 00:14:13.656
I like how they have a

00:14:13.656 --> 00:14:16.125
"not actual size" warning on this bag,

00:14:16.125 --> 00:14:18.094
just in case you thought that one crisp

00:14:18.094 --> 00:14:20.062
was the size of your head as well.

00:14:20.062 --> 00:14:23.399
Next up we've got Sizzling
Flame-Grilled Steak Max crisps.

00:14:23.399 --> 00:14:24.500
Now, these ones I'm interested by.

00:14:24.500 --> 00:14:25.868
These are Max crisps,

00:14:25.868 --> 00:14:29.305
and they are double
crunch KFC Zinger flavor.

00:14:29.305 --> 00:14:30.840
I think in the UK, we have a sort of

00:14:30.840 --> 00:14:33.075
hot chicken sandwich at
KFC called a Zinger burger,

00:14:33.075 --> 00:14:35.945
and supposedly these
are flavored like that.

00:14:38.014 --> 00:14:40.583
Little Guy Fieri flames on the chip there.

00:14:40.583 --> 00:14:41.450
Yeah, pretty good.

00:14:43.052 --> 00:14:45.187
See, the flavor is not very strong,

00:14:45.187 --> 00:14:47.490
but they're not kidding
on the double crunch.

00:14:47.490 --> 00:14:50.660
This is like [crunching],

00:14:50.660 --> 00:14:53.195
"I'm a man! I want to take
my crunching to the max!

00:14:53.195 --> 00:14:54.630
Bleh!" Like, this is —

00:14:54.630 --> 00:14:56.866
If the Zinger crisps somehow
weren't enough KFC for you,

00:14:56.866 --> 00:14:58.968
then we also just have a kind of standard

00:14:58.968 --> 00:15:01.304
KFC Max crisp as well.

00:15:01.304 --> 00:15:04.240
The next one we have is this
Fiercely Flamin' Hot flavor.

00:15:04.240 --> 00:15:06.776
Then we've got a few Max Strong crisps,

00:15:06.776 --> 00:15:07.910
which I think are Walkers' attempt

00:15:07.910 --> 00:15:10.513
to market to quite a specific demographic,

00:15:10.513 --> 00:15:13.416
which is mostly male, a little bit older,

00:15:13.416 --> 00:15:16.185
and kind of, like, the
blokey, laddie types.

00:15:16.185 --> 00:15:18.821
And it says "perfect with
beer" underneath. Like ...

00:15:18.821 --> 00:15:20.356
Putting the marketing to
one side for a second,

00:15:20.356 --> 00:15:21.457
they come in three flavors,

00:15:21.457 --> 00:15:25.094
which are hot chicken
wings, fiery peri-peri,

00:15:25.094 --> 00:15:26.562
and jalapeño and cheese.

00:15:26.562 --> 00:15:28.631
Then our final three Max
flavors are these three,

00:15:28.631 --> 00:15:30.499
which are loaded cheddar and onion,

00:15:30.499 --> 00:15:31.801
bold barbecue ribs,

00:15:31.801 --> 00:15:34.370
and XXL chicken and chorizo flavored.

00:15:34.370 --> 00:15:37.006
You can also get Lay's Wavy chips,

00:15:37.006 --> 00:15:39.342
which is their shameless
rip-off of Ruffles.

00:15:39.342 --> 00:15:41.177
And with Wavys, they come in flavors

00:15:41.177 --> 00:15:42.912
of reduced-fat original;

00:15:42.912 --> 00:15:44.380
original, which I think are these;

00:15:44.380 --> 00:15:45.748
I brought the ranch!

00:15:45.748 --> 00:15:48.351
Hickory barbecue, salt and
pepper, and lightly salted,

00:15:48.351 --> 00:15:49.952
and one that I think is limited,

00:15:49.952 --> 00:15:51.320
because it says on the bag.

00:15:51.320 --> 00:15:52.388
Look what I found.

00:15:52.388 --> 00:15:54.757
I don't even think
Harry knows I got these.

00:15:54.757 --> 00:15:58.361
Carnitas street tacos Wavys.

00:15:58.361 --> 00:16:00.429
Hell yes.

00:16:00.429 --> 00:16:03.632
Whoa, smells good.

00:16:04.467 --> 00:16:05.768
Oh, smells real good, actually.

00:16:07.403 --> 00:16:08.938
Uh-oh. These aren't that good.

00:16:08.938 --> 00:16:12.708
Trying to get flavored carnitas and onion

00:16:12.708 --> 00:16:14.744
and cilantro and lime

00:16:14.744 --> 00:16:16.345
all in a chip is very difficult.

00:16:16.345 --> 00:16:18.547
Good effort, guys, good
attempt, but I mean ...

00:16:18.547 --> 00:16:19.815
Next up we've got Sensations,

00:16:19.815 --> 00:16:22.818
which is Walkers' range of
slightly more upmarket crisps.

00:16:22.818 --> 00:16:24.954
They come with this very
sleek black packaging.

00:16:24.954 --> 00:16:28.023
They have the kind of slightly
fancier flavor descriptions.

00:16:28.023 --> 00:16:29.959
So, the classic Sensations
come in four flavors,

00:16:29.959 --> 00:16:30.893
which are as follows:

00:16:30.893 --> 00:16:33.863
got this one, which is
hickory-smoked cheddar and bacon.

00:16:33.863 --> 00:16:35.798
This one, which is
roasted chicken and thyme,

00:16:35.798 --> 00:16:36.866
personal favorite of mine.

00:16:36.866 --> 00:16:38.534
And we've got this one,
which is balsamic vinegar

00:16:38.534 --> 00:16:39.902
and caramelized onion.

00:16:39.902 --> 00:16:41.637
And a firm crowd favorite on the end here,

00:16:41.637 --> 00:16:43.606
which is Thai sweet chili Sensations.

00:16:43.606 --> 00:16:45.274
Now, finally, Sensations also offer these

00:16:45.274 --> 00:16:47.376
lime and coriander chutney Poppadoms.

00:16:47.376 --> 00:16:49.178
Also in the US you can
get something called Stax,

00:16:49.178 --> 00:16:51.380
which is this. It's not
so much, I don't think,

00:16:51.380 --> 00:16:55.618
unique flavors, it's just
a different chip vessel.

00:16:55.618 --> 00:16:57.820
Clearly, Lay's is going after Pringles.

00:16:57.820 --> 00:16:59.321
I mean, they're all
going after each other.

00:16:59.321 --> 00:17:02.158
These chip brands, man,
they are cutthroat.

00:17:02.158 --> 00:17:04.860
Let's find out how good of a job

00:17:04.860 --> 00:17:07.396
the Stax do

00:17:07.396 --> 00:17:10.766
protecting their chips.

00:17:10.766 --> 00:17:13.002
Did that really do that good of a job

00:17:13.002 --> 00:17:14.603
protecting these chips?

00:17:14.603 --> 00:17:16.205
They're still, some of them are broken.

00:17:16.205 --> 00:17:18.774
Ooh, Buffalo wings with ranch. All right.

00:17:18.774 --> 00:17:20.976
Xtra Flamin' Hot, Yuelei.

00:17:20.976 --> 00:17:22.445
Ready to turn it up?

00:17:24.213 --> 00:17:25.381
Surely you jest.

00:17:25.381 --> 00:17:26.582
These are not spicy at all.

00:17:26.582 --> 00:17:27.883
Whoa, major letdown.

00:17:27.883 --> 00:17:31.320
That's Xtra Flamin' Hot,
and this is Flamas Xtreme.

00:17:31.320 --> 00:17:34.223
But different colors, and
it's worded differently.

00:17:34.223 --> 00:17:35.524
Jesus.

00:17:35.524 --> 00:17:37.092
If you saw this color in the wild,

00:17:37.092 --> 00:17:39.161
you're in trouble. Turn around and run.

00:17:39.161 --> 00:17:41.030
Spicy Chile Limón.

00:17:41.030 --> 00:17:44.099
It's like, how do we make our
chips worse on your palate

00:17:44.099 --> 00:17:45.634
and worse for the environment?

00:17:45.634 --> 00:17:47.670
Ta-da. Stax were born.

00:17:47.670 --> 00:17:48.504
Avoid.

00:17:48.504 --> 00:17:50.406
Other flavors I was not
able to get my hands on

00:17:50.406 --> 00:17:53.175
by time of filming this: bacon
and cheddar potato skins,

00:17:53.175 --> 00:17:55.911
mesquite barbecue, and Flamas.

00:17:55.911 --> 00:17:59.215
Poppables, which is them
going after Doritos 3D,

00:17:59.215 --> 00:18:02.117
and Doritos 3D was just
Doritos going after Bugles.

00:18:02.117 --> 00:18:03.486
They got four flavors.

00:18:03.486 --> 00:18:05.354
I got all four. I can't believe it.

00:18:05.354 --> 00:18:08.123
Those flavors are sea salt,

00:18:08.123 --> 00:18:09.325
sea salt and vinegar.

00:18:09.325 --> 00:18:12.027
Yo, what's up?! Salty!

00:18:12.027 --> 00:18:13.596
Honey barbecue.

00:18:13.596 --> 00:18:14.797
White cheddar.

00:18:14.797 --> 00:18:17.333
I don't want to try these at
all, but I feel like I should.

00:18:17.333 --> 00:18:19.201
What is this?

00:18:19.201 --> 00:18:21.737
It's like a little, like, chip pod.

00:18:23.372 --> 00:18:25.074
What is the point of this?

00:18:25.074 --> 00:18:26.475
I don't like Poppables.

00:18:27.877 --> 00:18:29.111
We do have Stax in the UK,

00:18:29.111 --> 00:18:30.946
but they're marketed under
the Doritos brand name

00:18:30.946 --> 00:18:32.448
rather than the Walkers brand name.

00:18:32.448 --> 00:18:33.649
We also used to have Poppables,

00:18:33.649 --> 00:18:35.451
but it seems like they've
recently been discontinued.

00:18:35.451 --> 00:18:37.219
That said, we do have a bunch
of other exclusive snacks

00:18:37.219 --> 00:18:38.821
marketed under the Walkers brand name.

00:18:38.821 --> 00:18:39.922
We'll start with Wotsits,

00:18:39.922 --> 00:18:42.224
which I think are like
our equivalent of Cheetos.

00:18:42.224 --> 00:18:43.726
We used to be able to
get Cheetos in the UK,

00:18:43.726 --> 00:18:45.060
but then they got taken off the shelves.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.362
Basically what we have are these, like,

00:18:46.362 --> 00:18:48.864
baked cheesy puff snacks.

00:18:48.864 --> 00:18:50.065
The standard flavor is cheese,

00:18:50.065 --> 00:18:51.367
which is this blue one here,

00:18:51.367 --> 00:18:53.936
but they also come in
the form of Flamin' Hot.

00:18:53.936 --> 00:18:56.805
And you can get both flavors
either as a small version

00:18:56.805 --> 00:18:58.407
or as a giant version.

00:18:58.407 --> 00:18:59.508
Next up we've got Monster Munch,

00:18:59.508 --> 00:19:02.444
which are these kind of
puffed corn, maize snacks

00:19:02.444 --> 00:19:04.079
in the shape of a monster claw.

00:19:04.079 --> 00:19:04.914
And you can get them flavored

00:19:04.914 --> 00:19:07.182
with either pickled onion, roast beef,

00:19:07.182 --> 00:19:08.117
or in Flamin' Hot,

00:19:08.117 --> 00:19:09.718
which unfortunately I couldn't find today.

00:19:09.718 --> 00:19:10.953
Just like Wotsits, you can get them

00:19:10.953 --> 00:19:13.322
as the regular size or as the giant size.

00:19:13.322 --> 00:19:14.323
Next up we've got Quavers.

00:19:14.323 --> 00:19:17.560
These are kind of like a
thin, puffed curly snack,

00:19:17.560 --> 00:19:19.562
and they usually come flavored with cheese

00:19:19.562 --> 00:19:21.630
but are also available as salt and vinegar

00:19:21.630 --> 00:19:22.965
or as prawn cocktail versions.

00:19:22.965 --> 00:19:24.533
And then finally we have Squares.

00:19:24.533 --> 00:19:26.602
Squares are these very thin,

00:19:26.602 --> 00:19:28.237
as you can imagine, square-shaped crisps.

00:19:28.237 --> 00:19:30.973
Very crunchy, usually quite
flavorful. I quite like those.

00:19:30.973 --> 00:19:32.641
And they come in salt and vinegar,

00:19:32.641 --> 00:19:34.710
cheese and onion, or ready salted.

00:19:34.710 --> 00:19:36.245
Lay's also makes dips.

00:19:36.245 --> 00:19:39.048
Creamy jalapeño, smooth ranch dip,

00:19:39.048 --> 00:19:40.916
and, of course, French onion.

00:19:40.916 --> 00:19:43.319
Yuelei says cheddar and sour cream.

00:19:45.588 --> 00:19:47.356
Yeah, that's really good.

00:19:47.356 --> 00:19:48.691
We also have a couple more crisp options

00:19:48.691 --> 00:19:50.259
sold under the Walkers
brand name in the UK

00:19:50.259 --> 00:19:51.894
which unfortunately we couldn't get today.

00:19:51.894 --> 00:19:54.930
These include French
Fries, Bugles, and Mixups.

00:19:57.066 --> 00:19:58.367
Are there any questionable ingredients

00:19:58.367 --> 00:20:00.202
to look out for in your
Lay's and Walkers chips?

00:20:00.202 --> 00:20:02.037
As far as the basic salted version

00:20:02.037 --> 00:20:03.872
of Lay's chips go, we're fine.

00:20:03.872 --> 00:20:05.341
Both in the US and the UK,

00:20:05.341 --> 00:20:06.742
they are simply made up of

00:20:06.742 --> 00:20:09.211
potatoes, vegetable oil, and salt.

00:20:09.211 --> 00:20:10.512
But when you venture into other flavors,

00:20:10.512 --> 00:20:12.114
things can get a little more interesting.

00:20:12.114 --> 00:20:13.148
For example, in the UK,

00:20:13.148 --> 00:20:15.451
several of our flavors
contain potassium chloride.

00:20:15.451 --> 00:20:17.186
In normal doses, this is a perfectly safe

00:20:17.186 --> 00:20:19.021
low-sodium alternative to salt.

00:20:19.021 --> 00:20:20.889
However, it's also one
of the three ingredients

00:20:20.889 --> 00:20:23.626
used in the three-drug
cocktail for lethal injections.

00:20:23.626 --> 00:20:25.060
Enough potassium chloride in your system

00:20:25.060 --> 00:20:27.496
will lead to an irregular
heartbeat and a cardiac arrest.

00:20:27.496 --> 00:20:29.365
We don't have that in our USA Lay's,

00:20:29.365 --> 00:20:31.634
but we do have caramel
color in our barbecue

00:20:31.634 --> 00:20:33.135
and honey barbecue chips.

00:20:33.135 --> 00:20:34.169
Ah, caramel color.

00:20:34.169 --> 00:20:36.372
It is a widely used food coloring,

00:20:36.372 --> 00:20:37.740
and it's also a controversial one.

00:20:37.740 --> 00:20:40.376
Certain types of caramel
color can contain a byproduct

00:20:40.376 --> 00:20:44.413
called 4-Me upper-case I. That's not an L.

00:20:44.413 --> 00:20:47.483
Studies show that it caused
cancer in rats and mice,

00:20:47.483 --> 00:20:49.184
leading to campaigns in support

00:20:49.184 --> 00:20:51.787
of banning it in foods. Makes sense.

00:20:51.787 --> 00:20:53.889
The FDA stopped short of banning it,

00:20:53.889 --> 00:20:57.493
claiming that humans don't come
close to levels of exposure

00:20:57.493 --> 00:20:59.628
that caused the rats' tumors.

00:20:59.628 --> 00:21:01.263
Sounds like a challenge.

00:21:01.263 --> 00:21:03.032
But that didn't stop
the state of California

00:21:03.032 --> 00:21:05.701
adding it to its Proposition 65 list

00:21:05.701 --> 00:21:08.837
of chemicals, quote, "Known
to the state of California

00:21:08.837 --> 00:21:12.174
to cause cancer or reproductive
toxicity," end quote.

00:21:12.174 --> 00:21:13.008
Another fun thing to note

00:21:13.008 --> 00:21:14.977
is that our smoky bacon
and roast chicken crisps

00:21:14.977 --> 00:21:16.979
are actually both
suitable for vegetarians.

00:21:16.979 --> 00:21:18.714
The flavoring is just
made up of other things

00:21:18.714 --> 00:21:20.149
and doesn't include any meat extract.

00:21:21.917 --> 00:21:23.719
Which country has the
least healthy crisps?

00:21:23.719 --> 00:21:25.020
Let's compare the classic first.

00:21:25.020 --> 00:21:27.790
A 28-gram bag of classic Lay's in the US

00:21:27.790 --> 00:21:30.659
contains 160 calories.

00:21:30.659 --> 00:21:32.494
If we scale up the UK's 25-gram bag

00:21:32.494 --> 00:21:34.029
to account for that extra 3 grams,

00:21:34.029 --> 00:21:38.167
28 grams of UK ready salted
would contain 147 calories.

00:21:38.167 --> 00:21:41.670
So per gram, the UK's crisps
are healthier in every metric.

00:21:41.670 --> 00:21:42.738
OK, fine,

00:21:42.738 --> 00:21:45.007
but what about the least
healthy chip in each country?

00:21:45.007 --> 00:21:46.475
Over here, a lot of them are tied

00:21:46.475 --> 00:21:49.078
at 160 calories per 28-gram bag,

00:21:49.078 --> 00:21:52.347
but we did find that of
the 160-calorie chips,

00:21:52.347 --> 00:21:53.916
the highest fat content

00:21:53.916 --> 00:21:55.851
are in the cheddar and sour cream.

00:21:55.851 --> 00:21:57.186
Obviously the smaller bags.

00:21:57.186 --> 00:21:59.088
That makes them the least healthy.

00:21:59.088 --> 00:22:00.389
The least healthy crisps in the UK

00:22:00.389 --> 00:22:02.791
are the Strong hot
chicken wings Max crisps.

00:22:02.791 --> 00:22:05.127
28 grams of these would contain ...

00:22:05.127 --> 00:22:06.562
Honestly, my main
takeaway from this is that

00:22:06.562 --> 00:22:08.831
crisps might not be as unhealthy
as I thought they were.

00:22:08.831 --> 00:22:11.166
You could eat, like, 10 multipack
bags of the ready salted,

00:22:11.166 --> 00:22:12.935
and the only daily limit
you would have exceeded

00:22:12.935 --> 00:22:14.470
would be your fat intake.

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:17.539
Yes, Harry, I believe that's
called death by deliciousness.

00:22:17.539 --> 00:22:18.574
I live by the motto,

00:22:18.574 --> 00:22:22.277
"Live fast, die fat, and
leave a salty corpse."

00:22:22.277 --> 00:22:24.046
That's actually my LinkedIn headline.

00:22:24.046 --> 00:22:25.414
Have you ever seen that thing about how

00:22:25.414 --> 00:22:27.516
if you look at the KFC logo,

00:22:27.516 --> 00:22:29.051
it looks like a stick-man body

00:22:29.051 --> 00:22:31.120
with the head of Colonel Sanders on it?

00:22:31.120 --> 00:22:32.454
Is there anything worse
than when you're hungry

00:22:32.454 --> 00:22:33.489
and you're like, "I'm
gonna try something new,"

00:22:33.489 --> 00:22:34.523
and it stinks?

00:22:34.523 --> 00:22:36.125
You don't even stop being
hungry because you're full.

00:22:36.125 --> 00:22:38.427
You're, like, no longer hungry
'cause it tasted so bad.

00:22:38.427 --> 00:22:40.896
Ugh, that's the worst. That's this.

00:22:40.896 --> 00:22:44.433
I don't know if XXL is
referring to the crisps,

00:22:44.433 --> 00:22:47.603
the size of the packet, or the
chickens that they're using.

00:22:47.603 --> 00:22:48.804
Look at how red that chip looks.

00:22:48.804 --> 00:22:51.807
Like [growls].

